<title>LEBANON: Lebanon banks' balance sheet rises in Q3 - report.</title>
<headline>Lebanon banks' balance sheet rises in Q3 - report.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consolidated balance sheet of Lebanon's commercial banks rose to 33,353 billion Lebanese pounds by the end of the third quarter, the Lebanese Banks' Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The association grouping 82 commercial banks said in its report for October the banks' balance sheet rose 5.6 percent in the three months from June when they stood at 31,573 billion.</p>
<p>In dollar terms, the balance sheet rose to $21,401 million at the end of September 1996 from $20,097 million in June, the report added.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures (in billions of Lebanese pounds unless otherwise stated).</p>
<p>				    Sept 96    June 96    Sept 95</p>
<p> Consolidated balance sheet 33,353     31,573	27,887</p>
<p>Consolidated</p>
<p>  balance sheet ($mlns)     21,401     20,097	17,316</p>
<p> Total deposits		 27,946     26,568	23,482</p>
<p> Lebanese pound deposits    11,947     10,873	 7,680</p>
<p>Foreign currency</p>
<p>  deposits ($mlns)	    10,266	9,990	 9,812</p>
<p> Loans to private sector    12,376     11,969	10,013</p>
<p> Loans to public sector     10,083	8,992	 6,172</p>
<p>--Beirut editorial (9611) 353078 645456 602057</p>
</text>
